# Brickworks in French (Français): the words of the interface, chosen in
# Settings, Language (src/ui/language.gd). Every word the app draws is written in
# English; each entry here is one of them, as msgid, and how it reads in this
# language, as msgstr.
#
# An entry with %s or %d in its msgid is a pattern: any words, or a number, in that
# place, put into the msgstr's own %s or %d in order ("%2$s" names the second).
# A row's key after its words, a tooltip's lines, and "…" at a row's end are
# matched without entries of their own; so is a row's words with its first
# letter lowered, as the keys sheet writes them.
#
# The LEGO® names for parts, as the LEGO Group's own French pages write them:
# brique, plaque, plaque lisse, brique inclinée, tenon, plaque de base, minifigurine, instructions de montage, étape, sous-ensemble. LEGO® stays an adjective. Colours keep LDraw's and
# BrickLink's names, as BrickLink Studio does in every language; keys keep the
# names the menus write them with (Ctrl, Shift, Alt, Esc, Enter).
#
# src/dev/languages_probe.gd says which words have no entry (--missing=FILE).
msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Project-Id-Version: Brickworks\n"
"Language: fr\n"
"MIME-Version: 1.0\n"
"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\n"
"Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n"

